Local-first code review tool

Usage:
  stet [command]

Available Commands:
  benchmark   Measure model throughput (tokens/s) for the configured model
  cleanup     Remove orphan stet worktrees (not the current session's worktree)
  commitmsg   Generate a conventional git commit message from uncommitted changes using the local LLM
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  critic-eval Score past findings with the System One critic and recommend systemone_min_keep
  dismiss     Mark a finding as dismissed so it does not resurface
  doctor      Verify environment (Ollama, Git, models)
  finish      Finish the review session and remove the worktree
  help        Help about any command
  list        List active findings with IDs (for stet dismiss)
  optimize    Run optional DSPy optimizer (reads history.jsonl, writes system_prompt_optimized.txt)
  rerun       Re-run full review (all hunks) with current or overridden parameters
  run         Run incremental review (only to-review hunks)
  skill       Print Agent Skill Markdown for LLM integration
  start       Start a review session at the given ref (default HEAD)
  stats       Impact reporting (volume, quality, energy)
  status      Report session status (baseline, findings, dismissed)

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for stet
  -v, --version   version for stet

Use "stet [command] --help" for more information about a command.
